    list come from _data/dataModel.js; the rules themselves are only in CONVENTIONS.md. -#}
<div class="entity entity--full">
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="small mb-2"><a href="/data/">Data</a> › Data model</nav>
  <h1 class="mb-3">Data model</h1>
  <div class="reading-column ms-0">
    <p class="lead">Every find, analysis, site and publication is a record with its own IRI under
    <code>https://lod-am.net/id/</code>. The diagram shows the main kinds of records and how they link.</p>
    <p>It is an overview for orientation. The modelling rules, with every class and property, are in the
    <a href="https://github.com/LOD-AM/knowledge-graph/blob/main/CONVENTIONS.md">LOD-AM conventions</a>.
    To try the links out, start from the <a href="/query/examples/">example queries</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <figure class="mt-4" aria-labelledby="model-caption">
    {% include "lodam/model.njk" %}
    <figcaption id="model-caption" class="small text-body-secondary mt-2">
      Boxes with a coloured edge are records with their own pages, each linked to its list; plain boxes are parts of
      a record (a find's sample, an analysis's measurements); dashed boxes are concepts of other vocabularies. The
      dashed line is a path the model has but the released data don't use yet: a find known only by its site points
      to the site's place. Dates belong to contexts: a feature (or a site without features) is dated to a phase, and
      a find takes the date of its context.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <details class="mt-3 reading-column ms-0">
    <summary>The diagram as text</summary>
    <ul class="entity-list mt-2">
      {%- for e in dataModel.edges %}
      <li>{{ e.fromTitle }} → {{ e.label }} → {{ e.toTitle }} ({% for p in e.props %}<code>{{ p }}</code>{% if not loop.last %} or {% endif %}{% endfor %}){% if e.note %}, {{ e.note }}{% endif %}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </details>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-5" id="vocabularies">Ontologies and vocabularies</h2>
  <p class="reading-column ms-0">The released data use these ontologies and vocabularies. Getty AAT, ChEBI, Wikidata
  and ROR concepts are reused by their own IRIs. PeriodO and Pleiades are part of the model, but no released record
  uses them yet.</p>
  <div class="table-responsive">
    <table class="table table-sm entity-table model-vocab" aria-labelledby="vocabularies">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Vocabulary, version and namespace</th><th scope="col">Used for</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for v in dataModel.vocabularies %}
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">{% if v.url %}<a href="{{ v.url }}">{{ v.name }}</a>{% else %}{{ v.name }}{% endif %}{% if v.version %} <span class="text-body-secondary fw-normal">{{ v.version }}</span>{% endif %}<br><code class="model-ns">{{ v.ns }}</code></th>
          <td>{{ v.usedFor }}</td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
